From 065946a77c016eeff2e096ba22bca192bddef7f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: novahe <heqianfly@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 01:31:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Implement asynchronous startup memory prefilling for VM
 restores

This commit implements asynchronous startup memory prefilling using recorded
page access profiles (startup-profile.json) to proactively load hot pages,
reducing UFFD demand fault latency and optimizing VM restore performance.

Key Enhancements & Architectures:
1. Asynchronous Prefill Engine:
   - Spawns concurrent background workers to read profiles and prefetch
     hot memory ranges right after Cloud Hypervisor starts.
   - Obeys user-defined timeout limits and memory budgets (MaxBytes).
2. Direct PTE Installation:
   - Uses UFFDIO_COPY via `ioctlUffdCopy` on Guest VAs instead of copying
     via sandbox-ctl's mapped `backendVA`.
   - Installs EPT page tables directly for the Guest, yielding zero UFFD
     faults and zero userspace context-switch overhead for prefilled pages.
3. StateMap Synchronization:
   - Tracks page state transitions (Absent/Loaded/Released) using a
     shared PageStateMap.
   - Prevents duplicate reads and copy EEXIST attempts by setting state
     to Loaded after successful prefilling.

Safety & Race Condition Defenses:
1. EVENT_REMOVE / StateReleased Race Defense:
   - Implements pre-check and post-copy CAS logic in PrefillCopy.
   - If Guest ballooning/free-page-reporting frees a page concurrently (triggering
     EVENT_REMOVE and StateReleased) during UFFDIO_COPY, prefiller skips
     the page and refuses to overwrite or forcibly punch holes, relying on
     atomic CAS to preserve safe semantics.
2. Bounds Validation Overflow Fix:
   - Implements overflow-safe bounds validation on profile ranges to
     prevent malicious profiles (with large offsets/lengths wrapping to 0)
     from bypassing checks and causing out-of-bounds panics (DoS).
3. Budget Overshoot Race Fix:
   - Uses stable, upfront static reservation (selectRanges) before spawning
     workers to strictly enforce MaxBytes under heavy concurrency.
4. Polling Loop CPU Waste Fix:
   - Refactors the uffdHandler ready check loop in serveandwait.go to
     listen to backendCtx.Done() via select, avoiding up to 5 seconds of
     wasted polling when CH is terminated early.
5. Hot Path Recorder Optimization:
   - Skips the O(256) absentRunFrom page scanning when StartupRecorder
     is active, eliminating redundant StateMap accesses during demand recording.

Signed-off-by: novahe <heqianfly@gmail.com>
